Archie: a sticky bottom section and a search box in the sidebar.

The bottom of the vertical tab strip stays pinned to the bottom of the
sidebar and holds, from top to bottom:
  - a pill showing the previously active tab (click to switch back) and a
    button that scrolls the tab list to the active tab;
  - Back, Forward and Reload buttons (dimmed when unavailable) and the new
    tab button.
The new tab button opens a floating search box (ArchieCommandBar) instead
of a blank tab. It shows address-bar style suggestions while you type,
from the omnibox's own autocomplete engine (history, bookmarks, open tabs,
search suggestions). Up/Down pick one, Enter or a click opens it in a new
tab, Esc or clicking elsewhere closes the box. Middle-click (paste and go)
and the new tab button's context menu still work.

A footer at the very bottom has a settings button (Patch notes, Check for
updates, Browser settings) and an "Update available" warning that
appears when the Archie repository on GitHub has a newer release than
the running version (ArchieUpdateChecker). Clicking it opens the patch
notes (ArchiePatchNotes), which list every release's notes and link to
the download. archie_version.h is generated by scripts/prepare.sh.

